lines=['# Existing crypto15m design on five additional assets','','## Clear decision','','Do not add any of the five to live trading yet. DOGE is the only first-priority forward-paper candidate under the unchanged design. BNB has severe feed continuity problems; NEAR and ZEC lose in the opening-quote replay; HYPE has too few observations. These are conclusions about the current design and this sample, not all possible strategies on these assets.','','## Exact strategy and period','','September8 00:00 to September26 00:00UTC exclusive:18days,1704 retrieved settled markets per asset,8520 total. Expected every-quarter-hour grid has1728 closes per asset;24 per asset are absent from the reused public-history collection and their cause has not been verified. No result is claimed for missing markets. Reused Kalshi inputs are in ../kalshi_full_review_2026_09_26/candidate_data. All450 Coinbase request batches are retained locally.','','Rules are unchanged from deployed scanner: favorite ask85c–below93c, spread<=2c,3–10minutes left,61 consecutive completed Coinbase minute closes for60logreturns, population standard deviation, Coinbase pre-open close as strike proxy, signed cushionz>=2. Missing minute bars invalidate signals; no forward fill. All five current USD products were returned online by Coinbase. Contract metadata names CF Benchmarks asset-specific60second averages; Coinbase closes remain a proxy. Actual Kalshi settlement labels determine wins/losses. Two contracts per simulated trade. Fees use quadratic multiplier1, rounded to0.0001dollar. Tick-rounded cap is signal ask+1c, maximum93.9c. One entry per market, held to settlement.','','## Results: next-minute opening ask proxy','','Opening quote is an optimistic availability proxy, not proof of a fill after the signal. +1c/+2c costs are stress deductions per contract on top of spread/fees, not actual limit prices.','','| Asset | Trades | Wins/losses | Fee-only net | Net +1c | Net +2c | First9d / second9d (+1c) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
